   "html_text": "In general, in Latin American countries the philosophy of science began to be cultivated in the mid-twentieth century in those academic circles that were favorable to analytic philosophy, understood in a broad sense. The so-called “philosophical analysis”, more than a school or doctrinal body, represented in Latin America an alternative way of doing philosophy: in this trend, the methodological demands of conceptual elucidation and argumentative rigor supported a reaction against the metaphysica",
